/** Only observed releases and tested candidate changes. No inferred v1–v8 history. */
export function ChangelogView(){return `<article class="about changelog"><a class="back-link" href="#start">Back to your classroom idea</a><h1>Changelog</h1><p>Changes to this independent CoSN CVAT adaptation. Interface releases are separate from the original workbook’s version.</p><section aria-labelledby="text-capacity-release"><h2 id="text-capacity-release">Version 12 · Text capacity and Excel verification</h2><p><time datetime="2026-10-23">October 23, 2026</time>. Independent verification completed.</p><p>Free-text fields now accept up to 32,767 UTF-16 code units. Oversized input is rejected without truncation. Native Excel edit, save, reopen and app import checks passed at 20,001 and 32,767; file-size guards also cover complete maximum-length drafts. Scoring, original questions and design are unchanged.</p><p><strong>Independent verification:</strong> all 20 baseline capability groups passed, 100/100 on the defined equally weighted rubric. Fresh Excel 16.114 recalculation, pivot refresh, save/reopen and app import passed across seven synthetic workbooks. This is bounded CVAT capability parity, not vendor approval or universal Excel/browser compatibility.</p><p>Native Excel re-encodes the shared CoSN logo while retaining its picture objects and readable content. Original app exports preserve the source media; byte-for-byte identity after native saving is not claimed.</p></section><section aria-labelledby="mobile-release"><h2 id="mobile-release">Version 11 · Mobile navigation</h2><p><time datetime="2026-10-22">October 22, 2026</time></p><p>Phones and portrait tablets now use a compact Menu button instead of stacked header links and a full navigation rail. The drawer includes all assessment pages, workbook sections, help, source notes and exports, with a clear current page.</p><p>The menu supports keyboard focus, Escape, Close, outside-tap dismissal and return focus. Assessment responses, calculations, local drafts, dictation and Excel exchange are unchanged.</p></section><section aria-labelledby="candidate-release"><h2 id="candidate-release">Version 10 · Complete analyst workflow</h2><p class="release-status"><strong>Interface version 10.</strong> Release prepared <time datetime="2026-10-21">October 21, 2026</time> (Central). Source workbook: CoSN K-12CVAT Lite 4.1.</p><ul><li>Restored all 59 answer-dependent workbook guidance formulas.</li><li>Added district analyst calculations, manual company review, reasoned applicability and the complete six-framework crosswalk.</li><li>Added editable Excel import/export that preserves original sheets and separate analyst work.</li><li>Fixed large-backup round trips and date-formatted Excel values importing as serial numbers.</li><li>Linked exported answer and analyst summaries to their original input cells; conflicting edits are reported before import.</li><li>Added a complete printable assessment record and this dated changelog.</li></ul><p><strong>Verification:</strong> Source calculations and exchange were tested with synthetic records. Native Excel 16.114 open, edit, recalculation, save, reopen and app re-import passed with synthetic records; all 12 original tabs were checked. A later independent review found the text-capacity gap addressed in the version 12 update above. Its completed independent verification is described separately; this is not a universal compatibility claim. No result certifies or approves a vendor.</p></section><section aria-labelledby="live-release"><h2 id="live-release">Version 9 · Previous release</h2><p><time datetime="2026-10-21">October 21, 2026</time></p><p>This earlier release introduced the teacher intake and IT request, all 76 original fields, vendor evidence notes, optional device-only drafts, backup/export and browser dictation where supported.</p><p>The version 9 update corrected header contrast and typography across routes, enlarged important helper text and improved responsive/enlarged-text readability. The new analyst calculations and editable Excel exchange above are not part of version 9.</p></section><section aria-labelledby="workbook-release"><h2 id="workbook-release">Source workbook · Lite 4.1</h2><p>The original workbook’s ChangeLog records <time datetime="2024-03-01">March 1, 2024</time> for version 4.1. Its release history is preserved in exported workbooks; these interface changes do not change CoSN’s source version.</p><p><a href="#about">Source, attribution, license and documented workbook inconsistencies</a></p></section></article>`;}
